# The generated files in `data/` are validated byte-for-byte against the
# sha256 and byte count recorded in `data/manifest.json`. Git's autocrlf on a
# Windows checkout rewrites every newline and the file no longer matches the
# manifest that describes it, so `npm run validate` fails on a clean clone
# while CI, which runs on Linux, stays green.
#
# Normalise to LF everywhere. The pipeline writes LF, so this keeps the
# working tree identical to what was hashed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
